README.OSK -- Boa 0.92p on this diskWHAT SHIPS  CMDS/NETWORK/boa     the archive's own binary, byte for byte                       (OSK/CMDS/boa, 70,432 bytes).  Built by the porter                       with Ultra C; it links `csl' and `math', which ship.  /dd/c/unid/boa/osk   the server root.  The path is compiled in as                       /h0/C/UNID/BOA/OSK, so a bare `boa' finds it when                       this disk is also /h0.  CONF/boa.conf, CONF/mime.types,                       HTML/index.html, and logs/, which must be writable.NOT REBUILT, and why: the makefile links Microware's ISP socklib.l, whichis not in the SDK used here, and the binary works as it is.CHANGES  CONF/boa.conf        the porter's own file is kept as ORIG/CONF/boa.conf.                       Port 80 -> 8080 (a host port needs no privilege);                       User/Group 99 -> 0 (no passwd entry needed);                       ServerName added (boa stops at start-up without one:                       "Cannot determine hostname.  Set ServerName");                       DocumentRoot and ScriptAlias moved to this disk's                       paths; the porter's own Alias lines removed (they                       named directories on his machine); DirectoryCache                       /r0/tmp -> /dd/tmp.  /cgi-bin/ runs WN's CGI                       examples, which are on this disk with their source.  HTML/index.html      new, a short page saying where it came from.  OSK/CMDS             not copied here: test.cgi and query_results.cgi are                       built on cgihtml, whose source and terms are not in                       the archive; ptxm is a different copy from the one                       already on this disk; sigchild's author is unknown                       and boa runs without it.  The source in ADDONS stays.  DOCS/dummy           an empty placeholder, dropped.No source file was changed.RUNNING IT  boa &                          serves /dd/c/unid/boa/osk/HTML on port 8080  boa -c <dir> &                 another server root: <dir>/CONF/boa.conf                                 and <dir>/CONF/mime.types, and <dir>/logs  Stop it with kill <pid>; it finishes its requests and exits.  Text files go out as they are on disk, with CR line ends; the porter's  readme.boa says browsers accept that and a text client may not.